My friend told me of a site I could use to search for apartments in Dubai called PropertyFinder(specifically
propertyfinder.ae
), which was a pretty good site. Although finding proper accommodation that wasnt expensive was a bit difficult and most of the time far away from the Campus.

I mean my situation was quite unique because it was a two-semester Erasmus exchange, so the classes by and large were OK for registration, but I had to renew my pre-approval application from UCPH so often that it itself became a challenge to make all ends fit. On one occasion the registration messed up however, as there were multiple classes at AUD for the same course, and the person at AUD registering me put me on the correct course but the wrong class - which collided with the timing of another course I also applied for, meaning I couldn't get in, and by the time I found out, there were no spots left on that course. But overall it was OK, their course overview (such as this:
https://online.aud.edu/Campus/fall2023ug.asp
) was very well done with clear overview of courses, schedules, spots left, room numbers, and later on exam dates.
